==Acquisition==
Brief Respite is dropped by the [[Orphid Specter]], available upon anointing a Silver Grove shrine with the [[Apothic#Twilight|Twilight Apothic]].

==Drop Locations==
{{DropLocations}}

==Notes==
*Stacks with the [[Set_Mods#Augur_Mod_Set|Augur]] mod set effect for a total of 390% Energy to shield conversion.
*{{WF|Inaros}}, {{WF|Nidus}},  {{WF|Kullervo}}, {{WF|Hildryn}} and {{WF|Lavos}} (due to having either no energy or no shields) gain no benefit from this aura.
*Shields are only replenished from activating abilities. Constant Energy drain from channeling abilities or triggered drain such as {{A|Artemis Bow}} shots do not replenish Shields.
*Because the amount of shields restored is based off energy usage, this means that [[Ability Efficiency]] can ''reduce'' the amount of energy this Aura sees spent on most abilities.
**Conversely, equipping {{M|Blind Rage}} to decrease Efficiency increases the effectiveness of the aura.

==Trivia==
*Brief Respite was the first (and is currently the only) aura possessing the {{Pol|Zenurik}} Zenurik polarity.
**The only Warframe to possess a default {{Pol|Zenurik}} Zenurik aura polarity is {{WF|Dagath}}, who released seven years after Brief Respite was introduced.
**{{WF|Dante}}, {{WF|Jade}} and {{WF|Protea}} ({{WF|Protea Prime|Prime}}) possess a default {{Pol|Aura}} Universal aura polarity, the only other Warframes who "match" Brief Respite by default.

==Bugs==
*In the [[Simulacrum]], triggering this aura fully restores shields, then grants overshields proportional to energy spent. 
**[[Augur Set|Augur Mods]] do not share this bug.

